On Thursday, March 04, 1999 6:45 AM, Michael Tibor
[SMTP:tibor@lib.uaa.alaska.edu] wrote:
> I'm having problems getting CMU-SNMP and MRTG running on my as200.
I've
> built cmu-snmp-3.6 and mrtg-2.6.4.  At the moment, my problem seems to
be
> snmp:
> 
> [root@alpha /root]# snmpwalk localhost public
> Error building packet
> An error occurred, Quitting
> 
 I had exactly the same thing when i tried it. On further
investigation it looks like cmu-snmp is very much *not*
64-bit clean and is going to require a lot of work to get
it there.
  In my experience it seems to be that the software that
breaks most when you try and compile on/port to the axp
tends to be network software: generally because every
time they've built their own packets dubious assumptions
have been made about the size of integers.

cheers
john


