On Thu, 4 Mar 1999, Tom Holroyd wrote:

> On Wed, 3 Mar 1999, Greg Lindahl wrote:
> 
> >> >I'm running 2.2.2-ac4, AlphaPC164LX, Adaptec AHA-294X...
> >> >dd if=/dev/zero of=/tmp/moo bs=10240 count=10000
> >> >and the system froze right after it finished.
> >
> >The problem seems to be with multiple disks. The tester was talking
> >about having 2 disks, and during his dd tests, he may have had enough
> >disk access on the other disk to trigger the bug.
> >
> >I have the buggy driver on 67 machines, and it's never crashed a
> >system with only one disk in use.
> 
> I disconnected all the external disks and it still happened.  I tried
> going back to aic7xxx driver version 5.1.10, but that didn't help either. 

There's one thing I haven't seen mentioned in this thread. I don't
know if this is still the case with Adaptec, but a few years ago, they
were putting out a new revision of the firmware on a _very_ frequent
basis, (read: fixing bugs and inserting new ones) and they didn't
always update the firmware version numbers. It wouldn't surprise me in
the least that this may, in some way, be the cause of many people's
problems - it's not trivial to write drivers for `N' (where N is very
large) different versions of the `same' card/firmware.

Just my $0.02

Carpe viam,
Mike

