On Wed, 10 Mar 1999, Bruce Embrey wrote:

> I have an AS200 that comes up in SRM console. I have the fwupdate.exe
> to update the bios but do not have a boot disk that srm can read. When I
> use a fat formatted disk with the fwupdate.exe and try to boot, I get an
> error. The boot command I am using is boot dva0. The message I get is:
> 
> (boot dva0.0.0.0.1)
> block 0 of dva0.0.0.0.1 is not a valid boot block
> bootstrap failure
> 
> I need to run the fwupdate to install the arc console so I can dual
> boot NT and Linux. Any help is much appreciated.
> 
> Bruce

Keep your FAT16 disk with fwupdate.exe. Get another floppy, get mkboot.exe
from 
gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/utility/ run mkboot.exe from a
dos/windows system (or use the equilvilant dd if=) and use fwupdate.exe as
the image to be put on the floppy. Then place the new disk in the AS200
type 'boot dva0' which will get you to arc, take the disk out and replace
it with the FAT16 disk and choose update firmware from the arc menu, After 
it's done, power the AS200 off for 10 minutes then turn it back on and you
should be running arc.


HTH,

Ron Farrer



