You would need your LAN folks' help to make a static WINS entry. This is
will be easiest thing to do.

However my Samba expert buddy says you can make a non-static entry to the
WINS Server without their help by running SAMBA on your LinuxBox and
configuring SAMBA with correct WINS address for your network.  To find out
the WINS Server address, on a Win95/98 box on the same network segment as
your Linuxbox type: WINIPCFG at a command prompt,  or on WinNT type;
IPCONFIG /ALL.

Again, I haven't tried this.  Good luck.

Philip Chandy


