Couple of points:

a. sometimes, esp. with 100Mbit on 21142/21143, one has to resort to boot
   line args to force the tulip.c driver to handle a specific media type;
   check Becker's webpages WRT how this gets done.

b. AFAIK, the last de4x5.c driver I tried on XP1000 didn't like the new
   chipset (21143-PD or -TD, I can't remember which); this may have been
   updated since, so it would be worth a try via modules.

> 2. I seem to have either heat problems or the memory dimms
>    are not up to standard. I can't get the latest egcs1.1.2
>    to go thru a full build. It builds fine on my 164LX. I
>    get either core dumps at what appear to be random places
>    or I get a message something like "Unable to dup fd xxxxxxxx
>    to fd 0" while trying to copy the files to the installed
>    location. The first location looks obviously bogus.
>    Anyone seen that before??

Yes, and I'd say it's not memory-related, I see it on a DP264 as well,
and with older (1.0.3a) compilers. I suspect it's a bug in the EV6 support
around TLB/cache; I never saw this with older (2.1.120 vintage) kernels,
but ever since 2.1.130 or thereabouts, it's been annoying.

