The WEB page you  want is

http://cesdis.gsfc.nasa.gov/linux/drivers/tulip.html

Get the v0.90 Version from the above page, I have had no luck getting the
89H version to work on anything (on alpha). The 0.90 seems to work ok. I
have used it on DE500's and onboard tulips on Alpha Workstations and
Servers.


Your boot command would be similar to this, If using SRM/aboot

boot dk{something} -fi ?/vmlinux.gz  -fl "ether=0,0,*,eth0"

The -fl: "ether=0,0,*,eth0"  (with quotes) will select the media. 
where:
 something is your boot device/disk
? is the partition that contains your Linux Kernel
* is	0  (Auto-select)
	1  (10base2)
	2  (AUI)
	3  (100baseTx)
	4  (100baseT-FD)
	5  (100baseTx-FD)
	6  (100baseT4)
	7  (100baseFx)
	8  (100baseFx-FD)
	9  (MII 10baseT)
	10 (MII 10baseT-FD
	11 (MII autoselect)
	12 (10baseT - noautoselect)
	13 (MII 100baseTx)
	14 (MII 100baseTx-FD)
	15 (MII 100baseT4)


All the commands can be placed in environmental variables that SRM will
keep. So you would only have to type "boot" on subsequent reboots or
powerup's.

JJ 


