have a couple of questions.

Memory: being budget constrained, I think i'll go with just 128MB. Is
this enough? I know alpha code is a lot less dense than ia32, but
i've no idea by what magnitude. (64MB is fine for me on intel)

Booting:

it seems the only way to boot linux with AlphaBios based machines is
to have a small dos partition, (i gather alphabios only supports
FAT). This is ...ugly. Anyway round it? ie native ext2fs /boot.

Milo:

