milo builds seem to be built with old kernel versions, so i guess
there are issues with MILO flashed in the prom.

VGA has to be in a 64bit slot:

any way around this? seems like a bit of a waste of a 64bit PCI
slot.. are there patches available to get MILO to recognise VGA cards
in the 32bit slots?

Finally, and a bit OT to a linux-axp list:

Can you run DEC/Tru64 UNIX on the Samsung UX? I ..might.. be able to
get a cheap/free Tru64 license via work. (legit, don't worry). But i
guess you need SRM to boot dec-ux 4. does SRM support Samsung UX?
(it's very similar to the DEC RXP board isn't it?)
 
thanks,

Paul Jakma.



