So far I can tell that the effect I am seeing is _unrelated_ to sound
output!
Test was: Playing a video-CD using xreadvcd and mtvp with option '-a0' which
disables audio completely. I also checked with qps that mtvp did not open
the audio device at all -> it did not.
So audio is out of the game and we are back where we started.
My favourite guess are still pthreads. Any further opinions?
Another small proof for this theory is that threads are the only kind of
processes that are allowed to leave the processe's address space, i.e. two
threads can share data. This could explain crashes of unrelated processes
because a thread left it's address space but did not use the other thread's
addresses.
Possible testprogram: Generate two threads that heavily communicate via
shared memory. Maybe I'll do that tomorrow.

