Few people use those kernel mods; most folks use the latest redhat and
compile their own mpich, etc.

> (d) Is it worth the money for the performance level gained? (IIRC, Beowulf
> nodes based on 164s on some vendor pages are <$2500 each. My best guess on
> DP264 nodes would be closer to ~13k per node.)

I believe so. IF you can use Digital's compilers, the floating point
performance of the 21264 is quite good, which allows you to have
a superior performance/$. Fewer, more-powerful processors is usually a
scaling win, too.

