Why use the subject line "gcc bug on alpha"?  This is not a gcc bug.

Th problem seems to be that when you compile the kernel, there are
some asm() statements which put instructions from the BWX extension in
the ASM output, but then your 'as' doesn't know that your chip has
BWX so it's trying to expand tham as macros for earlier chips.

I gather you have a 21264 chip but your old 'as' doesn't know about it.
You can presumably just tell it that you have a 21164a instead, by
compiling with "-Wa,-m21164a".  Try that.

Bye,
  Rob.

PS: If you want, I can send you 'binutils-2.8.1.0.1-1.alpha.rpm' for RH4
    which will upgrade your 'as' to something slightly less old than 2.7.0.2.


