On Sat, 20 Mar 1999, Paul Jakma wrote:

> uhmm.. arcsbios. ok. How does ARCSBIOS differ to AlphaBios?

It's different. In some ways it looks like ARC BIOS... Well after all it
was their best at a copy of it.

>   
> who designed the UX? Digital or deskstation? And is it used in any
> DEC alpha systems? cause then i guess there must be an SRM available
> somewhere.

The UX call RPX164-2 (or -4 for 4MB cache :) aka ruffian then, was
designed and build by Deskstation Technology, Inc. (www.dekstation.com)
back in 1997, and was first available in or around November (I think) of
that year.

The ruffian is now made by Samsung/API and call the UX (AlphaPC 164UX).


No DEC (Compaq) doesn't use it in any of the past, present, or future
systems.

> 
> looks like i'll have to stick to linux.. :) 

Yes, the UX only runs Linux and Windoze NT (of course).



