Watch out!  In the meantime I run into situations where some extra
bytes showed up, in some cases, in images created with mkisofs.
That way I produced nice coasters without failures in write. 1/2 :-)

The solution I have was to use mkisofs from 1.8a17 release of cdrecord.
After that all problems vanished.  Still it turned out that version
numbers for mkisofs did not change but assorted interfaces did and I could
not just replace mkisofs in xcdroast as I initially planned.  I had simply
rip-off the whole thing and replace it in toto by 1.8a17 (current at the
time I was doing that).  After the change errors in mkisofs vanished and
I did not have any problems save one minor side-effect that a progress
bar for CD writing is broken.  It has now two positions - 0% and 100%. :-)

I exchanged some emails with Thomas N. about that.  He claims that
because of changes in cdrecord restoring a progress bar is not a simple
patch. Because he works on a total rewrite of xcdroast he was not in
a hurry to look at the issue and he was also reluctant to have
"development" cdrecord software in xcdroast.  I did not run into any
trouble with it but YMMV.

> It should work fine
> if you set CDR_FIFOSIZE to 3M.

This .alpha.rpm actually installs as xcdroast a small script which
sets CDR_FIFOSIZE to 4000k - a value which works fine on Alpha -
and execs "the real thing" so it is transparent in use.

If you are brave, and especially if you feel like hacking Tcl, and
what is fed to it, you may retrieve my version (.src.rpm only) from
ftp://ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca/pub/xcdroast-0.96e-3hd.src.rpm and run
'rpm --rebuild' on it.  OTOH if I would be doing that today I would
likely try to substitute source with the latest cdrecord release; but
this one works for me.  Once again - YMMV.

  Michal


