There is NO WAY to disable the builtin serial ports COM1 and COM2. Your
problems are most likely related to multiple serial chips responding to the
same addresses.

> - When the modem is on com3 (IRQ 4 or 5) I get the verbal responses but
> reaction to commands is slow (e.g. ATH1 takes at least 10 seconds to give
> a dialtone and return an OK).

I use COM3 and IRQ 5, and it works fine. The 10 second pause is a timeout
value, which indicates you're not taking interrupts. Did you do a "setserial"
to set the IRQ of COM3 appropriately?  You prolly have to set the jumpers on
the card so that it DOES NOT do PnP, but has a fixed COM port and IRQ.

Good luck.

