On Sun, Mar 21, 1999 at 11:12:49PM -0600, Wes Bauske wrote:
> I do have a comment about how gcc unrolls loops....

If you had to force unrolling with -funroll-all-loops,
it means gcc got confused about the loop latch.  Which
entirely explains any losage you see in the unrolling.

There have been some bug fixes related to latch detection
recently -- some of them stupid.  If you're not currently
using egcs cvs, give it a shot and see if it does better.


