Eric Dittman wrote:
> 
> I loaded SRM in my 164SX board this weekend to see if
> OpenVMS would load.  It wouldn't (halt code 7 in the
> PAL code), so I tried to reload AlphaBIOS.  I can get
> the AlphaBIOS to install and start, but after starting
> I get the message that the NVRAM is invalid and must be
> reset to default.  I hit "ENTER" and the system hangs
> and has to be powered off.  After powering back on I have
> SRM again (without it being loaded from floppy; I've
> disconnected every other storage device).  I can't even
> get the failsafe loader to load AlphaBIOS and keep it there.
> Any ideas?  I'd rather use AlphaBIOS to load Linux than try
> to get loading from SRM working.

Rename your MILO to fwupdate.exe and copy it to a FAT formatted 
floppy. Then switch on the failsafe boot jumper on the motherboard
and put the floppy in drive. The system must load from this
"Firmware update floppy". I used it 1000 times here, because i have
MILO in flash, and one can't _easily_ run MILO from MILO.

 Oleg.


