All,


In response to Paul Jakma:

...

	uhmm.. arcsbios. ok. How does ARCSBIOS differ to AlphaBios?

ARCSBIOS and AlphaBIOS are similar, in that both implement the ARC
firmware specification for RISC processors, originally created by MIPS
(now, SGI).  They differ in that ARCSBIOS was written by Deskstation,
and AlphaBIOS by DIGITAL (now, Compaq).
  
...

	Who designed the UX? Digital or deskstation? And is it used in
any
	DEC alpha systems? cause then i guess there must be an SRM
available
	somewhere.

The UX was designed by Deskstation, probably starting from the reference
design made available to OEMs from (then) Digital Semiconductor.  The UX
is not used in any DIGITAL (now, Compaq) system products, and there is
no SRM available for it.

...

Cheers,
jwl


