> Alpha-Penguins,
> 
> I'm curious what mail servers (besides sendmail) people are using on Linux
> Alpha.  And I mean a full service mail solution, including smtp, pop, imap.
>  Something with mailbox capabilities, an optional web front end for clients
> and for admin, etc.

We are an ISP, using sendmail+qualcomm popper on AlphaLinux for
the internal layer (talking only with users and with external
layer machines, not with the outside network).  No imap service,
no web front end for clients.  In-house developed web front end
for admin.

The external layer now runs sendmail on HPUX, but I have planned
to move it over to postfix/AlphaLinux as soon as postfix is out of beta.
It is unlikely but not impossible that we go to a commercial 
product, the biggest obstacle being probably integration with
existing admin tools.

furio ercolessi
