With regards to your message at 12:29 PM 03-18-99 -0500,
Jay.Estabrook@digital.com. Where you stated:
<<<snip>>>
>> 3. I added a Symbios 875J based UW SCSI to the system and
>>    it appears SRM does not see it or any devices attached to
>>    it. Is there something I can set to get that recognized by SRM?
>>    I'm currently booting off the floppy until I get that fixed.
>>    I'd like to boot from that card. Note AlphaBios does see the
>>    adapter. It is on Bus 0, so I guess it's not sitting across
>>    a PCI bridge or anything odd like that.
>
>I'm guessing that that's one of the NT-only cards; Intraserver has 2 models,
>using the NCR 875 chip, one of which doesn't work under DU, I'm told. I don't
>know why, but seem to remember something about shared interrupts? Sorry...
>
>--Jay++
Actually, 875J does work on Alpha. For example the Diamond Fireport40 has
worked for some time, although it is no longer available.
As for the Intraserver "versions" this is simply in their ROM. If you have
the Linux/NT version of an Intraserver SCSI card it does not work with
their UNIX driver, to prevent piracy. It does work in FSAT SCSI-2 mode, but
to use the UltraSCSI advanced driver for UNIX you need the card with the
proper ROM that allows it to load the driver and use it.

So, if there is a problem, it is in SRM. I have NOT seen the Fireport40 (
875J) be seen in SRM, though ARC and AlphaBIOS of more recent vintages work
fine with it. Some of the older ARCs ( like on the Cabriolet) did not like
it, but the ARC on an EB164 or AlphaBIOS on an LX are happy with it.


