>>> Maurice Hilarius said:
>
> Both _could_ have 2 PCI buses, but on the XP1000 there are no slots
> attached to the second one from what I have seen..

XP1000 does have 2 PCI busses.

IIRC, the top three slots (2 64-bit and 1 32-bit) are on PCI bus 0, and the
bottom two are behind a bridge on PCI bus 1. Note that there's also builtin
QLogic 1040C and 21143-PD chips on PCI 1 as well.

Oh, and don't forget, there's also some kind of ESS sound chip as well, but
that is behind the Cypress PCI-ISA bridge on PCI bus 0.

And here's some more info about the "chipset" you guys are talking about,
ie the 21272 core logic called TSUNAMI.

* The Cchip provides the interface from the CPU and main memory, and
* includes a general-purpose interface for the flash ROM and interrupts
* (TIGbus Interface).  One Cchip is used per system.

* The Dchip provides the data path from the CPU to memory and I/O. Two,
* four, or eight Dchips can be used in a system configuration.  Eight Dchips
* provide two 256-bit memory bus interfaces on the AlphaPC 264DP. XP1000 uses
* four Dchips to provide one 256-bit memory bus.

* The Pchip provides an interface to the peripheral component interconnect
* (PCI).  One or two Pchips can be used in a system configuration. Two
* Pchips can be used to provide two independent 64-bit PCI buses. AlphaPC
* 264DP uses two Pchips to support two 64-bit PCI buses running at 33 MHz,
* as does the XP1000.

--Jay++

