X-Mailer: Mutt 0.95.3i

Anton Ertl and I have produced a patch for MILO that enables 16 kB
D-cache on 21064A (the previous MILO versions always initialised the CPU
in 8 kB D-cache mode).  The patch and binaries are available from
ftp://genie.ucd.ie/pub/alpha/milo.

The binaries have been built from my MILO source tree, which is based on
Jay's latest release from gatekeeper and contains a lot of bugfixes,
enhancements and perhaps some new bugs.  There is also new unpublished DEC
BIOS emulator library in it, kindly provided by Jay Estabrook in binary
form.  The new library solves the problem with the official MILO
sources, which can't be build with the DEC BIOS emulator on anything
other than Redhat-4.2 system.

Nikita


