Tom,
	I would highly suggest that you link your programs with either ffm 
or cpml as the math library.   For some functions, GNU libm returns 
denormalized numbers. (Numbers close to zero, but a pain to handle.)  ffm
and cpml both round these really small numbers to zero.  

	Wether or not this is "holy", is another war.  For most applications, 
it will fix the FPEs, and the program will still get the "right" answer. 

--Phil

