I recently bought a Multia and I need a little help.  Thankfully, I'm only
new to Alpha's and not to Linux.  Here's the story so far:

When I bought my Multia it cam with Windows NT 4.0 Workstation installed.
Joy.  After a long and painful search I get a cdrom drive for it.  Works fine.
Now it's Linux Time!  Redhat 5.2 from the Redhat Linux Variety Pack.  After,
some starts and stops, and much curseing, I get basic Linux working.  Here
are the problems, I'm still stuck with:

1) NT on the brain.  Every time I power on, I get a message saying that I need
to change the boot menu before I can boot Windows NT.  Every Time!  Anyone
know how to send this warning to /dev/null like I sent NT?

2) XWindows problems.  Under NT, I was able to get 800x600 resolution on the
monitor with a problem.  But under Xwindows, nothing over 640x480.  I even did
the fairly risky act of borrowing another person's xconfig file.  No dice.
Two different monitors were tried and nothing over 640x480.  I checked the
error listing and there was a valid mode for 800x600 still present.  But 
every time I hit Ctrl-Alt-+ to changes to any higher resolution, the screen
goes blank.  Ideas?  I tried to find the video resolution jumpers as listed
in the Multia manual, but the jumpers aren't labeled.  ( there is a posible
canidate on the board but it's not clear on which jumper is which and the
correct direction to jumper is anyone's guess.  If anyone wants to see the
block in question, I can put a digital picture on a web page.)

Other than these two problems, it was a fairly normal first install.  Easier
than when I started with Linux on Intel with Slackware.

Thanks!
Mike


