> > 1) NT on the brain.  Every time I power on, I get a message saying that I need
> > to change the boot menu before I can boot Windows NT.  Every Time!  Anyone
> > know how to send this warning to /dev/null like I sent NT?

> remove winnt from your boot menu

That still won't necessarily fix the "problem".  ARC checks every boot
selection you have when you boot up.  For example, I have a Linux-HD
entry and a Linux-Floppy entry on my Multia.  Since I don't keep the
boot floppy in the Multia's drive all the time, ARC
"warns" me that I should check the boot selections before I can boot
NT.  After a few seconds, it goes on and boots the Linux-HD selection
as it's supposed to (mine is set to autoboot).  Of course, if there
*is* a boot WinNT option, it's safe to delete it. :)

I could just delete the Linux-Floppy boot selection, but on occasion
it's nice to have - e.g when testing out new kernels.

As for the video, at least I don't feel so dumb about the very same
issue I first had with my Multia.  I just didn't understand what "TGA
supports only one mode line" meant.  Means that you should only have
the modeline you want to use uncommented in the config file.  Or, in
Xconfigurator parlance, select only the resolution you want to use.

