On Thu, 25 Mar 1999, Peter Howell wrote:

> 	Firstly, let me say thank you, thank you, THANK YOU to everyone who
> helped me hunt down the necessary information on getting my ZLXp-E2 to
> work under linux.  I have have an almost fully operational linux box.
> The only thing I haven't been able to get running is X.

I'm using the XF86_TGA version 3.3.3 without problems (well, with one
problem, anyway ;)  I've attached my XF86Config.  Make sure you're careful
to change the monitor section to match your own.  Also, Thomas Leitner
posted here several months ago regarding an electrical design flaw in the
ZLXp-E2 controller.  Basically, you need to short red ground and green
ground together to get a nice stable display.  I did this non-destructively
by wrapping a piece of wire between these two pins in my monitor cable.
I included his original message below, as well.

cheers,
