Hmm..  As much as I'd like to know why it doesn't work, I suppose it's a
moot point because 2.2 does work and that's what we want.

Two other details we've ran into since then, however (with 2.2.4 and RH5.2
aboot):

1.) The SRM reboot doesn't seem to work properly.  We have built the kernel
for SRM and not to keep existing SRM setup.  At the end of the shutdown
cycle, we get of these messages:

reset_for_srm: bus 0 slot 0x6 SRM IRQ 0x5 changed back from 0x15
...more of similar...
reset_for_srm: bus 0 slot 0x6 SRM MEM/IO restored to 0x10191
...more of similar...

And then it hangs.  Once, it did get back into SRM, but the display was
half red/white and half black/white, and it was immediately trying to boot
ewa0 via MOP.  ?

2.) Aboot doesn't seem to be able to boot from the disk.  We have installed
aboot from RedHat-5.2 (which, IIRC is okay for 2.2 kernel/binutils) and are
using BSD disklabel.  I've done this part before so I'm pretty sure I have
things setup right.  We have an old unused DOS partition as partition 1,
then a swap, then an ext2.  We run swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx, we
need the "-f1" argument to overwrite a portion of the first partition.
When we boot from SRM, control passes to aboot as usual, but then is says
something about ext2_init ... too many groups(528).  Our root partition is
/dev/sda3.

Any ideas?

