> When we boot from SRM, control passes to aboot as usual, but then is says
> something about ext2_init ... too many groups(528).  Our root partition is
> /dev/sda3.
this does always happen with aboot and a partition that is larger than 2GB
unpack the source of aboot, apply all patches and grep for
"MAX_SUPPORTED_GROUPS". Current setting is 256 (for about 2GB).
The drawback with changing it to 1024 (eg) is, the binary grows.
The code needs to be rewritten to use something different than a static
array ....

