Oops, the instructions I gave you where for the other noname (AXPpci33).

Format one floppy disk as DOS. Take udbupd38.img and do 'dd
if=udbupd38.img of=/dev/fd0H1440 bs=10240', if you haven't do so already.

Stick the disk in the floppy drive and at the

>>>

prompt type 'update arc', after that has *completely* finished (it will
say when it's done), power the system off for 10 minutes. Then power it
back on and you should be in arc. If 'update arc' doesn't do anything,
then you'll need to get "arcboot.exe" and do a 'dd if=arcboot.exe
of=/dev/fdoH1440 bs=256k' on a DOS formatted floppy. Then type 'boot -arc
dva0' from the

>>>

prompt. At this point you should be in the ARC console. Goto 
"supplimentary menu",  take out the disk and put the other one
(udbupd38.img) in. Select "install new firmware", when the system return
to SRM console you'll see a APU prompt. Type 'update arc'. When it is
done type 'Q' and press enter. When it tells you to, power off you
system for 10 minutes. When you turn it back on you should be in ARC.


If that doesn't work let me know!



HTH,

Ron Farrer



