Well from just looking at the tv.sec&tv.usec return values one gets the
idea that CPU usage is going to be fairly precise ( somewhere in the
microsecond  level)

The actual usage seems to loop off 3 digits of precision.

Reading the kernel code, one see's that the precision is based on clock
ticks/jiffies intervals.

There appears to be no better way of getting precision accounting, as it
appears that all other sys functions are rooted in the clock tick,
rather that something with a betther precision ( ie # instructions
executed, a real-time clock.)  I suppose if u give up ur tick, u still
get charged for it - but only in whole tic units
