Hello everybody,

What package would you recommend to measure a relative performance of
an Alpha machine (LX164) running Linux (RedHat 4.2)? I've got a
cluster of such machines running stuff via PVM and I'm observing some
kind of performance discrepancy across the cluster.

I tried to use the nbench (a so-called new Byte benchmark), yet the
result it produced don't seem to have much sense - it does show
discrepancies, yet they are different for different tests, so it is
impossible to find out which machines have insufficient performance.
Besides, it only tests the CPU, not disk access.

I'm going to look at lmbench and HINT, but maybe anybody has other
suggestions. Basically, I want to test a couple things: CPU
performance, disk performance and (if possible) CPU cache usage and
utilization.

The situation is a bit more difficult, since the cluster is running in 
a 24x7 mode, so I'd rather not shutdown PVM and other programs (I
could run the test during a period of very low activity), but in the
worst case I'll just take hosts from PVM one at a time to test...

PS. BTW, any suggestions on how to test NFS performance. I'm trying to 
optimize the block sizes for NFS...

Thanks in advance,

-- 
