On 26 Mar 1999, Alexander L. Belikoff wrote:

> PS. BTW, any suggestions on how to test NFS performance. I'm trying to 
> optimize the block sizes for NFS...

Dunno of how to test NFS performance exactly, but since this is in a
clustering effort, why not look into other network file systems too? I'm
thinking specifically of Coda (Look at the 2.2 kernel), and maybe even
Samba?

Now.. here is a bit of a speculation..

Why not write a C program to recurse the contents of /usr/bin,
/usr/local/bin, /usr/lib, etc.. and dump all the contents to /dev/null,
maybe make some large temporary files with a dd if=/dev/zero .. if the
configs on the machines are similar this should give a good indication
of performance for reads.. as it involves opening/closing loads of files,
gets directory contents and large files.. all the stuff that a file system
will do, no?

Just a thought. 

