With regards to your message at 09:53 PM 03-27-99 -0500, Larry Snyder.
Where you stated:
>I have available to me a pair of Quantum 9.1's.  These are Atlas II
>series differential scsi (68 pin) disks.  Tekram says the DC390U2 
>supports 'low voltage differential' 68 pin devices.  I tried the
>jumper on the disk to 'force 8-bit mode' and an adapter, but the
>53C810 in the Mustang didn't recognize it.  I saw no referrences on
>Quantum's site to a 'low voltage differential' interface spec.  Is this
>a workable combination?  I've been away from the low-level h/w side
>for too long to decipher the current market-speak.
>TIA,
>-ls- 
UltraSCSI 2 or Low Voltage Differential (LVD) is considerably different
than original differential SCSI. If you hoope up differential devices to an
UltraSCSI or U2(LVD) controller you stand a definite risk of frying something.

There are NOT compatible.

What you need for these disks is a differential controller.


