Adrian,

	I also am using the NAG f90/5 compiler.  

	I have an UNSUPPORTED hack that I used to get it to work.  

It turns out that NAG actually uses gcc to do its linking.  

You have to compile all of the object files individually with NAG and then
link with the following command: 

/usr/bin/gcc -o output_file object1.o object2.o object3.o 
 -Wl,-rpath,/usr/local/lib/NAGWare /usr/local/lib/NAGWare/libf95.so /usr/local/lib/NAGWare/libf95.a -lcpml -lm

The final -lm is necessary because some unresolved symbols remain in the
NAG libraries. (atan2.. I think)  The CPML people know the problem and are
working on it. 

(This procedure also works for ffm) 

--Phil

Digital/Compaq:                     HPSD/Benchmark Performance Engineering
Phillip.Ezolt@compaq.com                            ezolt@perf.zko.dec.com


