I wrote a background shell script for my Sun that checks 'ifconfig -a' for
the presence of ppp every five minutes or so, and if it's not there,
restarts it.  The scripting is based on the file locations of the ppp
freeware, so adjust for linux accordingly.

Side note - I'm not sure how your copy of 'wc' might behave.  When I ported
this from SunOS to Solaris, I noticed that 'wc -l' in SunOS will report a
line if there is a null line or a character, whereas in Solaris 'wc -l' will
only report a line if there is an actual character on that line.  Again,
adjust accordingly.

It works fine for me...

