>>>>> "SteveCraft" == SteveCraft  <scraft@nothinbut.net> wrote:

SteveCraft> [...] set the resolution to 1024x768.  How do I go about
SteveCraft> that?  Is there just one file in /etc I have to
SteveCraft> manipulate? [...]

Yes, and that file is /etc/X11/XF86Config

At the end of the file are a set of "Screen" sections.  The one with
`Depth: 8' is the one you'll be using, since that's all the UDB can
do: change the `Modes' line to read `Modes "1024x768"' rather than
`Modes "800x600"'.  See the XFree86 documentation for more details
(starting with XF86Config(5)).

