Hello,

I've bumped into somthing strange. This weekend I connected my
girlfriend's
HP DeskJet 670c to the parallel port of my Miata. I got the printer to
work
(sort of). I noticed that the settings of the parallel port are Irq=7
and
IO=3BC on the Miata (it said in the alphabios system configuration).

conf.modules:
alias parport_lowlevel parport_pc
options parport_pc io=0x3BC irq=7

OK. When I print on this printer, the machine paractically freezes. The
video dies and opening a new session (telnet / rsh) is impossible.

I have a sneaking suspision that the videocard (Millenium 2) and the
par_port
are in conflict somewhere. The IO-ports of the videocard are quite close
to 
printerport:

03c0-03df : vga+

Then again, I could be completely wrong.

I though that it could help if I moved the par_port's IO address a bit
higher,
say to 0x378. But I've got no clue how to do that. I haven't found a way
how to adjust it in the alphabios, and I beleive that there aren't any
jumpers on the
mainboard that handle this...

alias parport_lowlevel parport_pc
options parport_pc io=0x378 irq=7

Is there also a way how to get ecp or epp working on the parallel port??

Thanks,

Stefan van der Eijk
