Hello,

Hmmm.. I kind of remember this from when I was
compiling XFree86 3.3.2 a while ago... I might be
totally wrong.. but if my memory serves me well,

the problem is that the egcs doesn't know about

__alpha and only knows about __alpha__ .... 

the the LinuxMachineDefines that you removed should
really have been replaced with something more sensible.


The way I got around it was grep thru all the files in
the source tree for __alpha and replaced them with
__alpha__ ...once I did that, everything was fine.

Sorry if this is totally unrelated... but I think this
is what I remember... and it was egcs-1.1.1 too..

D.

