> > I would like it, especially if I can play my Direct X games on it.  FX!32
> > barfs on this, em86 and such just are not efficient.  I would also
> > eliminate dual booting as I use a Win CAD program too.
> 
> Why do you think that Softwindows on Linux/Alpha would be more
> performant than em86? Wouldn't it be YAE (yet another emulator)?

em86 is a great emulator, but only lets you run x86 Linux binaries.
SoftWindows will let you run any Windows 9x, 3.x, or DOS app. including
DirectX apps/games. It does a complete emulation of the Pentium
processor. Have a look at <http://www.softwindows.com> for more
information.


