This must be a SIMM incompatibility problem.  I have Viking 60ns 64 MB
simms in my as200 and they work beautifully.

If a dram manufacturer has made a chip series that deviates too far from
the 60ns average, it may cause timing and access problems with the entire
memory bus.  General rule is to only use identical simms/chips in the same
bus.  AFAIK the as200 doesn't do bus interleaving, so it should work if you
have diff. simms/drams in another bus.

