Since a DS20 has the same main board as a DP264, here is
it's performance:

Copy 1077.0   Scale 1244.0   Add 1179.0   Triad 1323.0

Note it is significantly faster than the optimized XP1000
results. Don't know about your runs, but assuming you
set the compiler switches for best performance, the XP1000
is not a good substitute for a DP264. I'd rather have a
2 processor DP264 than two XP1000's.

Also, egcs can do significantly better if you want to
tweak the code so it's happy with it. The streams benchmark
is what I would term "naive" coding.

Obviously though, DUNIX cc is a very smart compiler and handles
this code well.


Wes


